tcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete for both nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledgement, observed disruption, changed boot identity, and recovered trust/service behavior. Fixed lifecycle boot identities independently agree with the executor observations. The main deficiency is operational hygiene—unused SSH access artifacts, unnecessary port 80 exposure, and extensive retained temporary files including private-key material.","limitations":["The lifecycle failed-service probe is systemd-specific and unsupported on Alpine; direct OpenRC status and post-restart service tests compensate for the task service, but do not provide a general final failed-service inventory.","Lifecycle snapshots did not inventory /root/.ssh, so retained SSH artifacts are established from the state-changing commands and absence of any cleanup in the complete timeline rather than an independent final filesystem probe."]}
